From 32cfdbd2ed11f3b74c3ac642e6a48287ba1e5a73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Local <hermes-local@r730-001>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:43:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(toolsets): resolve plugin-toolset validity via the
 blocking reader

hermes update printed four false warnings right after the config migration:
platform 'cli'/'discord' references unknown toolset 'graphify'/'semble'.

Plugin discovery runs on a background thread that overlaps CLI startup and the
post-update config migration. The two plugins whose register() installs a JIT
dependency (hermes-graphify, hermes-semble) are still importing at that moment,
so get_plugin_toolsets() lacks their keys and the persisted key cache holds the
same partial set. The platform_toolsets validator asked the NON-blocking
accessor for VALIDITY, so every toolset owned by a still-registering plugin
looked like a typo.

Fix: add plugins.get_plugin_toolset_keys() (joins in-flight discovery, bounded,
falls back to the persisted set when discovery yields nothing) and use it where
membership decides validity: toolset_validation.saved_toolset_resolver and
tools_config._get_plugin_toolset_keys. The non-blocking accessor stays for
callers that only EXCLUDE these names (cli_init_mixin), where a miss
self-heals; its docstring now says so.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_toolset_validation_plugin_keys.py (4) pins that a
stale nowait set no longer hides a live plugin toolset, that a genuine typo
still warns, and the discovery-empty fallback. Injection-verified: pointing the
resolver back at the nowait reader fails 2 of them.

No regressions: failing-set diff vs stashed baseline over
test_toolset_validation/test_config_check_diagnostics/test_cli_init/
test_tools_config/test_commands/test_quick_commands/test_plugins is identical
(50 pre-existing sandbox-IO failures both sides).
